  <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-3 group">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-navy py-2 list-none flex justify-between items-center">
      Which Dolphin module can use the Alfa Laval WHPX 405?
      <span class="text-gold ml-2 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">&#9660;</span>
    </summary>
    <p class="text-text-light mt-2 pb-2">The Alfa Laval WHPX 405 is one exact base-machine option for the Dolphin DMPX-014 centrifuge system; another is the MOPX 205. The module adds the frame, PLC controls, feed pump, heaters, and piping. The OEM diesel values are 3,700 L/h (16.29 US GPM derived) for WHPX 405 and 3,300 L/h (14.53 US GPM derived) for MOPX 205, both at 40 &deg;C and 13 cSt.</p>
  </details>
  <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-3 group">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-navy py-2 list-none flex justify-between items-center">
      What is the difference between the WHPX 405 and MOPX 205?
      <span class="text-gold ml-2 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">&#9660;</span>
    </summary>
    <p class="text-text-light mt-2 pb-2">The Alfa Laval WHPX 405 and MOPX 205 are different base machines in the same commercial size class. WHPX 405 is partial-discharge and lists 3,700 L/h (16.29 US GPM derived) for marine diesel. MOPX 205 is total-discharge and lists 3,300 L/h (14.53 US GPM derived) for diesel. Both records are at 40 &deg;C and 13 cSt.</p>
  </details>
  <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-3 group">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-navy py-2 list-none flex justify-between items-center">
      What applications is the WHPX 405 / DMPX-014 best suited for?
      <span class="text-gold ml-2 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">&#9660;</span>
    </summary>
    <p class="text-text-light mt-2 pb-2">The WHPX 405 / DMPX-014 is suited for small to medium throughput applications including diesel fuel polishing, pyrolysis-oil dewatering, waste-oil recovery, lube-oil purification, and hydraulic-oil cleaning. Non-diesel duties require application sizing from the actual fluid properties and separation target.</p>
  </details>
  <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-3 group">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-navy py-2 list-none flex justify-between items-center">
      What G-force does the Alfa Laval WHPX 405 generate?
      <span class="text-gold ml-2 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">&#9660;</span>
    </summary>
    <p class="text-text-light mt-2 pb-2">The Alfa Laval WHPX 405 operates at approximately 7,200 Gs of centrifugal force at rated bowl speed of 7,600 RPM. This high G-force enables separation of particles down to 0.5 microns and effective water removal from oil and fuel products.</p>
  </details>
  <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-3 group">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-navy py-2 list-none flex justify-between items-center">
      Can Dolphin Centrifuge repair or supply parts for the WHPX 405?
      <span class="text-gold ml-2 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">&#9660;</span>
    </summary>
    <p class="text-text-light mt-2 pb-2">Yes. Dolphin Centrifuge supplies genuine and compatible replacement parts, complete bowl rebuilds, and remanufactured WHPX 405 and MOPX 205 centrifuges. Each rebuilt unit is tested to factory specifications before shipment. Genuine OEM parts are made by Alfa Laval; Dolphin's compatible parts are made by other manufacturers to the same fit and function, so you can choose on price and lead time. Dolphin Centrifuge is an independent remanufacturer and is not affiliated with Alfa Laval. Contact us for parts availability and pricing.</p>
  </details>


